The following files are taken from that project and carry its copyright:

    proba/metrics.py    byte-identical to upstream (verified by diff)
    proba/window.py     code byte-identical; one docstring line names this
                        package instead of upstream's in its usage example
    proba/detector.py   code identical except the adapter loader, which
                        imported `quadrat.detectors.*` by hardcoded name and
                        now resolves `__package__`; the dynamically loaded
                        adapter module gets a `proba_adapter_` prefix instead
                        of `quadrat_adapter_`. Two further changes are in
                        docstrings only (usage example, directory name).
                        No behavioural change.

Each file carries a header stating what was and was not changed. The claim is
checkable: fetch the upstream file and diff it against ours with the four-line
provenance header removed.

They are kept unchanged on purpose. The whole claim of this harness is that a
number it produces on the Russian corpus is comparable with a number quadrat-ipi
produces on the English one; that only holds while the code deciding where the
threshold sits, what a cell is, and how an interval is computed is the same code.
Files outside the list above -- the data layer, the paths, the adapters, the
importer and the table renderer -- are this project's own.
